        "p": [
          "Success is rarely achieved on the first attempt. The path to greatness is paved with failures, and the key to overcoming them is perseverance. The proverb \"Try, try again\" teaches us that we should never lose heart if we fail. A perfect example of this is King Bruce of Scotland. After being defeated by his enemies multiple times, he lost all hope and hid in a dark cave. There, he watched a tiny spider trying to weave its web to the ceiling. The spider fell nine times but did not give up. On its tenth attempt, it succeeded. This small incident inspired King Bruce to fight one more time, and he finally won his kingdom back. Failure is not the opposite of success; it is a stepping stone to success. If we work hard and persistently chase our goals despite hardships, victory will ultimately be ours."
        ]
