                    "q": ". Analyse the sample essay 'The Hazards of Movie Going': the three ideas in the introduction, the topic sentence of each body paragraph, the signalling phrase in the conclusion, and how the introduction and conclusion are similar and different.",
                    "a": "Three ideas in the last sentence of the introductory paragraph: (1) problems in getting to and inside the theatre, (2) the theatre seating, (3) the behaviour of some movie-goers.\nTopic sentences: First body paragraph — 'One reason why people prefer watching movies on the TV rather than going to the theatre is the time required in reaching and getting inside the theatre.' Second body paragraph — 'Even if one manages to get a ticket, there is the problem of getting a good, comfortable seat.' Third body paragraph — 'Furthermore, there are numerous other problems one has to face because of the way that many movie goers behave.'\nSignalling phrase in the concluding paragraph: 'In short,'\nIntroductory and concluding paragraphs compared: They are similar because both mention the same three problems and the preference for watching movies at home. They are different because the introduction introduces the topic and states what the essay will cover, while the conclusion sums up the points and gives the final judgement that watching on TV is a better option."
