                "q": "5. In the following figures, name the complementary angles, the supplementary angles, and the vertically opposite angles:\n(i) Right triangle with the right angle split into c and d; angles a, b, e, f at the crossing of the two lines inside; h at the top vertex; g at the bottom-right vertex.\n(ii) Two triangles meeting at a point, with a right angle at the centre; angles a, b at the top; c, d, e, f at the centre; g, h at the bottom.\n(iii) Right triangle with the right angle split into c and d; angles a, b at the top-left vertex; e, f, g, h at the crossing of the two lines.",
                "a": "(i) Complementary angles: ∠c, ∠d; ∠g, ∠h\nSupplementary angles: ∠a, ∠b; ∠b, ∠e; ∠e, ∠f; ∠f, ∠a\nVertically opposite angles: ∠a, ∠e; ∠b, ∠f\n(ii) Complementary angles: ∠c, ∠d; ∠e, ∠f; ∠c, ∠e; ∠d, ∠f\nSupplementary angles: ∠a, ∠b; ∠g, ∠h\nVertically opposite angles: ∠c, ∠f; ∠d, ∠e\n(iii) Complementary angles: ∠c, ∠d\nSupplementary angles: ∠e, ∠h; ∠h, ∠g; ∠g, ∠f; ∠f, ∠e\nVertically opposite angles: ∠e, ∠g; ∠h, ∠f"
