                "q": "6. Find the degree measure for the angles marked x, y and z.\n(i) Three lines through a point; one angle marked 20° and one right angle marked.\n(ii) Lines through a point; one angle marked 35° and two right angles marked.\n(iii) Lines through a point; one angle marked 30° and two right angles marked.\n(iv) Lines through a point; angles marked 75° and 30° and one right angle marked.",
                "a": "(i) Angle between the vertical ray and the 20° ray = 90° − 20°\n= 70°\nx + 70° + 20° = 180°\nx = 180° − 70° − 20°\nx = 90°\n(ii) y + 90° + 35° = 180°\ny = 180° − 90° − 35°\ny = 55°\nAngle between the down-right ray and the horizontal = 55°\nx = 180° − 90° − 55°\nx = 35°\n(iii) x + 90° + 30° = 180°\nx = 180° − 90° − 30°\nx = 60°\nAngle between the west ray and the down-left ray = x = 60°\ny + 60° = 90°\ny = 90° − 60°\ny = 30°\nz + 30° = 90°\nz = 90° − 30°\nz = 60°\n(iv) Angle between the west ray and the up-left ray = 75°\nAngle between the up-left ray and the shallow ray = 90°\nx = 90°\nAngle between the east ray and the shallow ray = 180° − 75° − 90°\n= 15°\ny = 15°\ny + z = 180°\nz = 180° − 15°\nz = 165°"
